---
title: Oven-baked Sunday gravy
tags: [italian, pork, weekend]
cuisine: italian
time: 2 hours 10 minutes
source: Oven Baked Italian Sunday Gravy by Josie and Nina, https://josieandnina.com/oven-baked-sunday-gravy
---

Heat the oven to 375°F.

Season both sides of the @pork chops{2}(bone-in) with @garlic powder{},
@onion powder{}, @oregano{}, @salt{} and @ground black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Heat the @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a 5 1/2 quart #Dutch oven{} over medium heat.
Brown the chops ~{2%minutes} a side and set them on a plate.

Soften the @onion{1}(diced) in the oil ~{3%minutes}. Add the
@garlic{4%cloves}(minced) and cook until fragrant.

Pour in the @white wine{1/2%cup} and let it bubble ~{2%minutes}.

Stir in the @tomato paste{6%oz} with @salt{2%tsp} and some pepper, and cook it
in the wine and onions ~{2%minutes}, pressing it against the pot.

Add the @San Marzano tomatoes{56%oz}(whole, pureed) and stir until the sauce
is one even colour.

Add @garlic{4%cloves}(peeled, whole), @basil{6-8%leaves}, @sugar{2%tsp} and
the browned chops.

Cover and bake ~{1%hour}. Stir in @water{2%cup}, lower the oven to 300°F, and
bake covered ~{1%hour} more.
